<title>HONG KONG: Hong Kong handover to go live on Internet.</title>
<headline>Hong Kong handover to go live on Internet.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's handover of Hong Kong to China on June 30 is to go live on the Internet with 48 hours of video footage to mark the historic occasion.</p>
<p>Organisers hope the coverage could spark more traffic on the information superhighway than the popular chess clash between world champion Garry Kasparov and the &quot;Deep Blue&quot; computer.</p>
<p>The service, covering the official handover ceremonies and giant fireworks display, is being run by the state-funded broadcasting network and Hong Kong's Chinese University.</p>
<p>It can be accessed on http://www.rthk.org.hk.</p>
</text>
